block content
    h1 Hemorrhoids
    p Definition by #[a(href="https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/hemorrhoids/symptoms-causes/syc-20360268") Mayo Clinic]:
    blockquote Hemorrhoids (HEM-uh-roids), also called piles, are swollen veins in the anus and lower rectum. Hemorrhoids are similar to varicose veins. Hemorrhoids can develop inside the rectum, called internal hemorrhoids. They also can develop under the skin around the anus, called external hemorrhoids.
